# Emission-parity fixtures are hashed BYTE-EXACTLY (content_hash.sha256 in the handoffs
# section, compared against a frozen golden). A checkout under `core.autocrlf=true` — the
# Windows default — rewrites these LF-committed files to CRLF, changing every hash and
# failing test_emit_parity::test_full_parity with no code defect anywhere.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in BOTH directions, so the working-tree bytes are
# the committed bytes on every OS and every git config. Do not relax this to `text eol=lf`
# without checking: that still normalizes on the way IN, which is fine, but leaves a
# `core.autocrlf=true` clone's existing files needing a renormalize pass.
* -text
